  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 consistently outperforms pca_n2000 (0.650 vs 0.591 in multiprofile+avgpool), and transformer vs avgpool yields a negligible difference (0.653 vs 0.650). The encoder choice is the dominant RNA-side design decision, yet scgpt has not been tested. Question: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) directly compares scgpt vs scvi_n200 while holding profile setting and aggregation fixed, cleanly isolating the encoder effect. Why best next: The encoder axis shows the largest known variance (~6 pts) compared to aggregation (~0.3 pts), so resolving whether scgpt can match or beat scvi_n200 reduces the most important uncertainty. A favorable scgpt result would redirect the multimodal search; a negative result confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred RNA representation and lets us focus remaining budget on fusion/multimodal questions with confidence."
}

